FORMAT|nsq=nsq(x) is the sum of the squares of the coordinates of x, its squared norm; the bar notation is avoided because the bar separates fields|matrix=[[a, b],[c, d]] is a block or entry matrix, rows first; I_m the identity of size m|gaussian=a Gaussian integer re + im i is written re:im|tensor=(x) is the tensor product|ids=C0.n common conventions, 4D, 7D, 8D, OB (obstruction), TS (tensor claim); P rows are predictions, C rows conventions|claim_tags=MEASURED computed by this script (self-checks only); NAMED stated in the literature, not run here; DERIVED derived by hand from NAMED identities, not run here; CONJECTURE none|status=PREDICTION marks a statement the measurement will test; CONVENTION marks a choice the measurement uses or states that it changed|json=0
CONV|id=C0.1|case=all|name=clifford_sign|value=gamma(u) gamma(v) + gamma(v) gamma(u) = -2 <u, v> I, so gamma(xi)^2 = -nsq(xi) I (the Lawson-Michelsohn sign: Cl_n = Cl(R^n, -nsq), generators square to -1)|status=CONVENTION|claim=NAMED|json=0
CONV|id=C0.2|case=all|name=symbol|value=principal symbols with the factor i dropped: sigma(d)(xi) = xi wedge ., sigma(d*)(xi) = -iota_xi, sigma(pi d)(xi) = pi(xi wedge .) for a projection pi|status=CONVENTION|claim=NAMED|json=0
